.TH CTI-AGENT-SECRETS 1 "2026-11-21" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-agent-secrets \- move the fleet's secrets out of fleet.env into systemd credentials
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets status
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets import
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets set
.I NAME
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets remove
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Step 2 of splitting
.IR fleet.env .
Each secret is encrypted by
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
to this machine's TPM where it has one, into
.IR /etc/credstore.encrypted/NAME .
Each unit imports only the secrets its programs read
.RB ( ImportCredential= ),
and systemd decrypts them for that run only. A unit skips a credential that
is not stored, and every program falls back to
.IR fleet.env ,
so secrets move one at a time.
.PP
It never prints a value, and passes values to
.B systemd\-creds
on stdin, never on a command line. It stores only the secrets
.I settings.manifest
marks. Root only.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Each secret: stored as a credential or not, and whether
.I fleet.env
still sets it, with what to do next.
.TP
.B import
Encrypt every secret
.I fleet.env
sets and the store lacks.
.B \-\-dry\-run
says what would be stored. A value that uses
.B $
or runs over several lines is skipped with a note; store it with
.BR set .
.TP
.BI set " NAME"
Encrypt one secret, typed (not echoed) or piped on stdin. Also how a secret
is rotated: the next run of every unit uses the new value.
.TP
.BI remove " NAME"
Delete a stored credential. Programs fall back to
.I fleet.env
from their next run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/credstore.encrypted/
The encrypted secrets, 0600 root, in a root-only folder.
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/credentials.stored
Which secrets are stored, names only, for
.BR fleet\-config (1).
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/share/credentials.map
Which secrets each command needs; the
.B cti\-agent
wrapper gives a hand run the grants its timer has.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
done;
.B 1
a secret could not be stored or the manifest could not be read;
.B 2
bad usage, an unknown name, an empty value, or not root.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets import \-\-dry\-run
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets import
.br
.B sudo cti\-agent\-secrets set CLIENT_SECRET
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
.BR fleet\-config (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1),
RUNBOOK.md section 11n.
